# PROC PRINT listing layout (OPTIONS NOCENTER)
OBS_LABEL = "OBS"          # heading of the observation-number column
COL_GAP = " " * 4          # blanks between PROC PRINT columns
BLANK_AFTER_HEADER = True  # blank line between the column headings and the first observation


def _print_table(title_lines, columns, rows, page_size=PAGE_SIZE):
    """
    PROC PRINT listing with ASA carriage control.
    columns: list of (header, width, align) tuples; width is ignored because
             PROC PRINT sizes each column to its widest heading/value.
    rows: list of tuples of already formatted strings.
    """
    obs_width = max(len(OBS_LABEL), len(str(len(rows))))
    widths = [
        max([len(header)] + [len(row[i]) for row in rows])
        for i, (header, _, _) in enumerate(columns)
    ]

    def _cell(text: str, width: int, align: str) -> str:
        return text.ljust(width) if align == "left" else text.rjust(width)

    header_line = COL_GAP.join(
        [OBS_LABEL.rjust(obs_width)]
        + [_cell(header, width, align)
           for (header, _, align), width in zip(columns, widths)]
    )

    def _header_block():
        block = [("1" if i == 0 else " ") + t for i, t in enumerate(title_lines)]
        block.append(" ")                    # blank line between titles and headings
        block.append(" " + header_line)
        if BLANK_AFTER_HEADER:
            block.append(" ")
        return block

    lines = []
    header_block = _header_block()
    lines.extend(header_block)
    on_page = len(header_block)

    for idx, row in enumerate(rows, start=1):
        if on_page >= page_size:
            header_block = _header_block()   # new page: ASA '1' + titles + headings repeat
            lines.extend(header_block)
            on_page = len(header_block)
        lines.append(" " + COL_GAP.join(
            [str(idx).rjust(obs_width)]
            + [_cell(value, width, align)
               for (_, _, align), width, value in zip(columns, widths, row)]
        ))
        on_page += 1

    return lines





What changed from the old layout
No dashed line under the headings. PROC PRINT does not print one.
Blank line after the title and another after the column headings.
Column widths are the widest of the heading and the values in that table, not fixed 10 and 15.
Alignment: numeric headings and values are right-aligned, and character ones are left-aligned. STATUS, FINALSTAT and DESC are the character columns.
Separator: 4 blanks between columns, as in the standard PROC PRINT listing.
OBS column: right-aligned, with the row number continuing across pages.
Paging: each PROC PRINT starts a new page with 1. The title and headings repeat on every page, and a page holds PAGE_SIZE (60) lines.
Assumptions to check against a real SAS listing
Column gap of 4 blanks.
Blank line after the headings, which is the BLANK_AFTER_HEADER constant.
OBS in capitals, because the JCL runs SAS609. SAS 8 and later print Obs.
No date or page number on the title line. The program only sets NOCENTER, so this assumes your site runs with NODATE NONUMBER.

If a listing differs on any of these, only OBS_LABEL, COL_GAP, BLANK_AFTER_HEADER, or the title line in _header_block needs changing. Pasting about 12 lines of one product from SAP.PBB.NLF.BEHAVE.TEXT would settle all four. The values in each cell already follow SAS formatting: _best12 and . for missing, from the earlier report() change. Step 11 pads every line to 250 characters.
